# Public keys trusted to sign my commits, for `git log --show-signature` and
# `git verify-commit`. Without gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile pointing here, git
# reports "No signature" on correctly-signed commits -- it has no way to map a
# signature back to a principal.
#
# Public keys only; nothing secret lives in this file.
#
# Both identities are listed on every key because the same machine signs under
# either email depending on the repo's remote (see the stacklok includeIf in
# .gitconfig). namespaces="git" scopes the trust to commit/tag signing.
#
# Keep in sync with the SSH *signing* keys registered on GitHub:
#   gh api /users/jbeda/ssh_signing_keys

# Mac (~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub) -- GitHub title "SSH key (ed25519)"
